  "tokens": 213,
  "cover_text": "In a small bowl, combine fennel, capers, rosemary, orange zest, lime peel, and a pinch of salt. Add cucumber. Season with pepper. Refrigerate, until ready to serve.\nPrepare thinly sliced cheese slices. Sprinkle lettuce with cheese. Serve ice-cold. (Note: Hard cheese only serves on the spicy side, and hard cheese costs more and tends to break down more quickly than softer cheeses.)\nFrom Jennette: \"Makes 14 large thick slices, 2-3 medium sopes. (1 slice was rare..yet perfect when you butchered it with a cheddar and fresh fennel and + some chives). To freeze in ice cube trays, pour cheese to filling and freeze. The consumption of this dish is low so I expect that to be our only dish that really has frozen leftovers.\"\n\"With a little dark dressing, you add a lot of tender fennel and heat to flavors you'd get in a salad. If you don't take fennel out, it's about the worst salad you'd ever make. You have to soak it in",
